@bank all
// Head writer 0607: shelves, stock and the Wednesday delivery (the systems engineer's, plan-0607 "The right part from
// the right shelf"). TEXTS, except stores.keeper (crew, a bubble) and stores.delivery (Yara Esposito; see
// content/lines/esposito-yara.lines). {part} a part's name ("relay"), {shelf} a shelf's name ("Lights"), {n} {max}.

== stores.fetch
- Fetch a {part}: the {shelf} shelf.

== stores.wrong
- Not this one. {part}s live on the {shelf} shelf.

== stores.shelf
- {part}s: {n} of {max}

== stores.low
- low

== stores.empty
- none left: the machine shop can make one

== stores.job.unload
- Unload the Wednesday delivery

== stores.unload.cart
- Take a hover cart from the cart bay.

== stores.unload.crates
- Tap the crates in the cargo hold. The cart pulls them in.

== stores.unload.shelf
- Take the cart to main storage and tap any shelf.

== stores.unload.again
- {n} crates still in the hold. One more trip.

== stores.unload.done
- All unloaded. Every part is on its shelf.

== stores.late
- The Wednesday delivery is late. It should be in a day or two.

== stores.keeper
- Relays on Lights, filters on Filters. Easy.
- Four crates. Lovely. My back says otherwise.   #funny
- Mind the cart. It's got a mind of its own.
- New stock! Best day of the week, this.
- Count twice, shelve once. That's the rule.

// the job board: a small job the crew took at once ({name} is their first name)
== board.crew
- {name} on it
